# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EngCoach environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you have. The app RUNS with none of
# these set — it falls back to clearly-labelled development providers and tells
# you so in the UI. See README "Running without credentials".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- The coach model (REQUIRED for the real experience) ----------------------
# Without this the coach runs on scripted replies and the analyzer eval refuses
# to report a precision figure. https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Local models via Ollama (OPTIONAL, ADR-022) ------------------------------
# Run models on your own machine: zero cost, nothing leaves the device.
# Requires Ollama 0.5+ (https://ollama.com) and a pulled model.
#
# 1. Pick where each lane runs:  anthropic | ollama | scripted
# ENGCOACH_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama            # all lanes local
# ENGCOACH_PROVIDER_HOT=ollama            # or just the conversation (recommended first step)
# ENGCOACH_PROVIDER_COLD=
# ENGCOACH_PROVIDER_SESSION=
#
# 2. Pick the model. Most specific wins:
#      ENGCOACH_OLLAMA_MODEL_<LANE>  >  ENGCOACH_OLLAMA_MODEL  >  built-in default
#
# One model everywhere (the usual case) - must match `ollama list` exactly.
# llama3.2:3b is the built-in default: ~2GB, ~650ms per warm conversation turn.
# ENGCOACH_OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:3b
#
# ...or per lane. A small fast model for talking, a bigger one for the analyzer where
# accuracy matters and latency does not:
# ENGCOACH_OLLAMA_MODEL_HOT=llama3.2:3b
# ENGCOACH_OLLAMA_MODEL_COLD=qwen2.5:14b-instruct
# ENGCOACH_OLLAMA_MODEL_SESSION=
#
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
#
# BEFORE trusting a local model on the COLD lane, measure it:
#     npm run eval:analyzers -- --provider=ollama --model=<name> --limit=20 --gate
# (flags, not FOO=bar prefixes - that is bash syntax and does nothing on Windows cmd)
#
# ALREADY MEASURED (ADR-025): qwen2.5:7b-instruct scored 5.6% precision and flagged 9 of 10
# CORRECT sentences. Do not put a small local model on the cold lane. The conversation lane is
# fine locally; the analyzer is not.

# Hosted model tier (ADR-013). Most specific wins:
#     ENGCOACH_MODEL_<LANE>  >  ENGCOACH_MODEL  >  built-in tiered default
# See docs/COSTS.md §3 for what each configuration costs.
#
# One model everywhere (this flattens the per-lane tiering below - that is a valid
# choice, just an explicit one):
# ENGCOACH_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
#
# ...or per lane. Defaults shown:
# ENGCOACH_MODEL_HOT=claude-opus-5
# ENGCOACH_MODEL_COLD=claude-haiku-4-5
# ENGCOACH_MODEL_SESSION=claude-opus-5

# Hard daily spend cap in USD (COSTS.md §6 lever 7). Default 5.00.
# ENGCOACH_DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD=5.00

# --- Speech recognition (RECOMMENDED) ----------------------------------------
# Without this, recognition falls back to the browser Web Speech API, which
# gives text but NO word timings — so pace, pause profile and run length are
# unavailable, and every asr-prone correction is suppressed (ADR-018).
# https://console.deepgram.com
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# DEEPGRAM_MODEL=nova-2

# --- Text to speech (OPTIONAL) -----------------------------------------------
# Without this the coach speaks through your browser's built-in voice, which is
# free but noticeably worse. https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts

# Default coach voice (ADR-020). A provider-agnostic key, NOT a provider voice id:
#   female  -> "Maya"  (OpenAI 'sage': calm, warm, conversational)   [default]
#   male    -> "Aaron" (OpenAI 'ash')
# Each user can override this in Settings. Without OPENAI_API_KEY the browser speaks instead and
# we pick the closest matching voice it offers, saying so if there is none.
# ENGCOACH_TTS_VOICE=female

# --- Database (OPTIONAL) ------------------------------------------------------
# Leave unset to use the embedded PGlite database at ./.data/engcoach — real
# Postgres, zero setup (ADR-016). Set this to point at Neon, Supabase, or a
# local Postgres instead; it is the same schema either way.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/engcoach

# Where the embedded database and any retained audio live.
# ENGCOACH_DATA_DIR=./.data/engcoach
# ENGCOACH_AUDIO_DIR=./.data/audio
